    "proseDraft": "It was confirmed by Rosa, Kwame and Lena with recheck passed that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30, 17:00 CT with Lena's sections reaching Kwame by Thursday noon. Questions were raised in discussion about whether to attach the pen test summary and whether insurance requires the certificate itself or just the coverage amounts.\n\nConfirmed by participants\n- It was confirmed by Rosa, Kwame and Lena with recheck passed that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30, 17:00 CT and Lena's sections reach Kwame by Thursday noon.\n\nStated in the meeting\n- A question was asked about whether to attach the pen test summary or just reference it.\n- It was suggested to attach the summary letter and not the full report that needs an NDA.\n- The speaker said they would answer for both and flag it.\n- It was said there is already a mutual NDA and the speaker would double check whether it covers security documents.\n- It was said their procurement lead said they need it back next Friday.\n- It was said Kwame owns the questionnaire back to them next Friday.\n- The speaker said they would do the legal and insurance sections and pass them to Kwame to merge in.\n- It was said to put them in the shared folder and not email.\n- The speaker said they would let their procurement lead know it is in progress.\n- It was said the format is spreadsheet because the portal is being replaced.\n- A question was raised about insurance and whether they want the certificate itself or just the coverage amounts.\n- The speaker said they would ask when writing to procurement.\n- The speaker said they would ask when writing to procurement."
